<title>CHINA: China completes Huizhou crude oil dock.</title>
<headline>China completes Huizhou crude oil dock.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 1.46 billion yuan ($174 million) oil dock in southern China began operation recently, the Economic Information Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The project on Mabian island in Huizhou port in China's southern Guangdong province includes a 150,000 tonne berth and 180-km of oil pipeline, the newspaper said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
